146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (Like a lot of you, we spent August 7 watching merchant Lightning nodes get swept. A bug in BTCPay Server let attackers pull LND macaroons off merchant servers without logging in. With those, they closed channels and walked off with the funds. Foundation, Citadel21, IVPN and others were hit. \(IVPN's writeup is worth a read.\))
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (To be clear, we love BTCPay Server. It has done more for merchant adoption than almost anything, and the team responded fast. But that week made something obvious that was always true: keeping a live, spend-capable Lightning node on the same internet-facing machine that runs your shop is fundamentally pretty scary.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (So we built OpenReceive to take spending out of the picture entirely.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
