/E (Politics and Government- Public choice theory is the study of how incentives affect the behavior of politicians, voters, and government employees. It's produced such foundational concepts as rent-seeking behavior, concentrated benefits & dispersed costs, rational ignorance, bureaucratic incentives, regulatory capture, and the political-business cycle.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
