/E (Law and Criminal Justice- The incentives and tradeoffs inherent to plea bargaining, tort law, and litigation have all been studied extensively through an economic lens. Economist pioneered the concept of optimal deterrence \(i.e. how much punishment effectively disincentives a crime, without going too extensive\), and written extensively about the negative effects of drug prohibition.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
