/E (On the "yes" side, I'd say that economists sometimes put too much trust in their tools than is warranted.  Although their tools are correct, there are always some simplifying assumptions that are made---those simplifying assumptions are sometimes quite important and economists often fail to recognize that.  They are sometimes blinded to common sense and traditional wisdom because of that.  They may be too quick to devalue common sense approaches that don't have solid empirical evidence behind them. ...)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [20]
>>
