/P 123 0 R
/E (            Hong Kong will always have a very special place in my heart. I spent about half of my adulthood there and am still very fond of the place and its people. I argue that around 2014-2018, Hong Kong was the most important city in the world for Bitcoin trading, and exchanges like BTCC, Binance, Bitfinex, Bitmex, Crypto,com, FTX, OKX, and many others have called Hong Kong their home at some point. The second Bitcoin ATM was installed at a Hong Kong bar called "Bitpoint," where one of the oldest still functional Bitcoin meetups convened regularly.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 123 0 R
/E (Today, the community is still somewhat there, but Hong Kong no longer plays an important role in Bitcoin globally. There are no relevant exchanges left, no large-scale events of global appeal, there are no noticeable startups, and I'm not aware of any exciting tech coming out of the city. However, I'm very positively surprised to see the local merchant economy is once again growing, particularly among the struggling bars, and so I refilled my Lightning wallet and went out to find them.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
