/P 123 0 R
/E (back the next day. Meanwhile my situation has been somewhat resolved, as I am shown a photo of a Binance wallet, with a QR code of a Lightning invoice. I pay the invoice, which takes my node about thirty seconds for a 1149 satoshi fee. Once I pay I ask the clerk to check with her boss, who tells her over Telegram that my deposit was made and that she can pay out the cash. The woman seems deeply impressed over the speed, as usually it takes about 30-60 minutes until onchain funds are received and payouts can be made. She asks me why not more people are using Lightning, and I tell her that it's "still early." I calculate my fees and figure I paid about a 3% fee over the market rate for the service. I'm quite happy about that, and I know a bank debit card would charge you about the same, depending on the amount.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [14]
>>
